    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d580">

                <pb facs="0574" n="540" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg540"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Mr. Dupuy de Lôme.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-12-21"><hi rendition="#italic">December 21,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 327.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the note which I had the honor
                    to receive from you under date of the 15th instant in regard to the recent
                    voyage of the schooner <hi rendition="#italic">Silver Heels</hi>, I have to
                    inform you that the Secretary of the Treasury advises me that the collector of
                    customs at Wilmington, N. C., was instructed on the 16th instant to detain the
                    vessel in question until further advised and meanwhile to consult with the
                    United States attorney, who has been instructed by the Attorney-General to go to
                    Wilmington.</p>
                <p>An earlier communication to you of this information was prevented by an
                    inadvertence, which I regret.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
